{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And it shall be for a sign upon your hand.</b> The arm tefillin — a remembrance of the strength of the hand; and the head tefillin — a remembrance of the signs and wonders that HaShem performed before our eyes. As it is written in the parashah of Va'etchanan: ״ויתן אותות ומופתים בפרעה ובמצרים לעינינו״." "<b>Your hand.</b> The weaker hand, for the right hand is ready for every matter and is extended everywhere, since it is more active than the left — and it is not fitting that the divine names be placed upon it. Another interpretation: our Rabbis said, because the right hand is designated to bind the tefillin upon the left hand, and not the left upon the right; and in most places the left is called יד (hand)." "<b>And for totafot.</b> From the language of gazing, like ״ועינוהי מטייפין״, on account of ״וראו כל עמי הארץ כי שם ה׳ נקרא עליך״; and through seeing them they will remember the miracles. A good ordering, the parashah of Bo."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:39.292050009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}